# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The Go build context is the repository root, which is ~11 GB of Go module
# caches and build output plus a 78 MB node_modules. Without this file every
# one of the 7 Build matrix jobs uploads gigabytes to the runner before it can
# start, and the local checkout does not fit in the transfer budget.

# Everything the Go images do not need
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
apps/mobile/build/
apps/web/.next/
apps/admin/build/
libs/shared/typescript/*.tsbuildinfo
libs/shared/typescript/node_modules/

# Rust / Python toolchains and caches
services/rust/target/
libs/shared/rust/target/
**/target/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Generated protobuf stubs: Dockerfile.go regenerates them inside the image
# with `make -C libs/proto gen-go`, because libs/proto/.gitignore keeps them
# out of the repository.
libs/proto/gen/

# Root-level generated output, also produced by buf
gen/

# CI/CD state
.github/
.git/
.gitignore

# Docs and local environment
docs/
*.md
!README.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# k6 load tests and misc tooling sources, not needed to compile a Go binary
tools/
tasks/